  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday morning through next Friday)\nIssued at 243 PM EDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nThe extended periods begin Monday with The main frontal boundary \nfrom the short term still stalled across E and SE GA. Continued \nSouthwesterly flow will also keep gulf moisture streaming across \nthe area so diurnally driven shower and thunderstorm chances are \nexpected to continue across the area. With this frontal boundary \nstaying nearly stationary a few waves move north along it with one \nbecoming a weak closed low over NE GA Tue afternoon. This low gets \nabsorbed fairly quickly into the boundary and moves rapidly up the \neastern seaboard Wed. This front stalls along the GA coast through \nWed before being pushed back to the west as the Bermuda ridge begins \nto strengthen turning the overall SWLY flow to SERLY by Thu/Fri. \nCurrently the models show the Bermuda ridge axis forming across the \nCarolinas and North GA which would put us in southeasterly flow \naround the bottom of the ridge. \n\nInitial \"cooler\" high temperatures Monday and Tuesday will bring \nmore widespread 80s to low 90s. Temperatures will be on a gradual \nwarming trend, with highs in the 90s by the end of the week.",
